  "_": [
    "Shared truth table for the routing-target classifier. TWO implementations read a token and must agree",
    "exactly: js/classify.js (the badge in the rule builder) and _classify_target() in swg-panel-server (the",
    "authority, which buckets patterns for the node in cascade_plan). The node has no classifier by design.",
    "",
    "Written BEFORE either implementation, on purpose: a table derived from one of them only proves that one",
    "is self-consistent. Syntax is LOCKED in docs/PATTERNS-AND-EXTRA-FLAGS-PLAN.md §1.1-§1.3; kinds and the",
    "capability matrix live in docs/ROUTING-RULE-BUILDER-PLAN.md §4.1.",
    "",
    "kind      what it matches                            tier  example",
    "  ip       an address or range (bare IP -> /32)         -   1.2.3.0/24",
    "  asn      every range announced by an AS               -   AS62041",
    "  site     a name and everything under it               1   google.com   *.google.com",
    "  zone     a whole ending, all of it                    1   *.ru       (NO public-suffix list: *.uk covers bbc.co.uk)",
    "  first    the first part of the name is X              1   google.*",
    "  any      some part of the name is X                   1   *.google.*",
    "  starts   the text starts with X                       2   google*",
    "  ends     the text ends with X                         2   *google",
    "  contains the text contains X anywhere                 2   *google*",
    "  invalid  nothing anywhere; `why` is a stable code, the prose is each UI's own",
    "",
    "`value` is the canonical operand as stored: lowercased, trailing dot stripped, scheme/path removed,",
    "IDN punycoded, a bare IPv4 widened to /32, an AS token folded to as<digits>. Tier-2 operands keep",
    "their punctuation (`*yandex.*` contains the dot) because the scan is literal, and are ASCII-only:",
    "half a label has no punycode form, and the wire carries names already encoded.",
    "",
    "THE TIER-2 FLOOR IS HERE; the rest of the policy is not. Three characters, on all three Tier-2",
    "shapes (ROUTING-RULE-BUILDER-PLAN \u00a712.1) — a Tier-2 operand's blast radius is its LENGTH and",
    "nothing else, so `*ru*` reads as \"Russian sites\" and matches ruble.com, brutal.io and truecaller.com.",
    "It is a fact about the token alone, like the ASCII-only rule above it, so it belongs to the grammar",
    "and to this table; `*ru` was a valid `ends` here until it landed, and nothing can have routed on it",
    "because no engine has ever lowered a Tier-2 kind. The per-interface cap and the per-engine capability",
    "gate stay out: both ask about CONTEXT over a kind already decided, and folding them in would make the",
    "table answer two questions at once and drift the moment either policy moved."
  ],
